detectiteasy for Debian
----------------------

The package is built with the upstream CMake build system. Since 4.0.0, the
libraries bundled upstream (qwt, zlib, bzip2...) are used instead of the
system ones.

The data files (signature databases, translations, styles...) are installed
in /usr/share/detectiteasy by the detectiteasy-data package, read-only.

Only the main DiE database (db) has an updater. die-update, also run by the
"Update" button of the GUI, sees that /usr/share/detectiteasy/db is read-only
and installs the new database in ~/.local/share/NTInfo/die/db. Each data path
set to "$data/..." is looked up first in ~/.local/share/NTInfo/die, then in
/usr/share/detectiteasy, so the updated database takes precedence.

The "Update" buttons of the info, PEiD and yara databases only open the
download page in a web browser. The signatures folder has no update. To use a
newer copy, extract it in ~/.local/share/NTInfo/die/<info|peid|yara_rules>.

Paths saved as /usr/share/detectiteasy/... by packages up to 3.21 are turned
back into "$data/..." when the settings are loaded.

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 03:40:00 +0100
